1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,339
In an old apothecary shop on Candlewick Lane, a ghost still
keeps the shelves.

2
00:00:04,339 --> 00:00:09,389
This is The Apothecary's Ghost, my entry for the Ghost in
the Machine challenge.

3
00:00:09,389 --> 00:00:11,513
Ambrose Quill is a made-up character.

4
00:00:11,513 --> 00:00:16,165
He drifts through the shop, his eyes follow your mouse, and
when you hover a jar,

5
00:00:16,165 --> 00:00:18,487
he whispers a line of history.

6
00:00:18,487 --> 00:00:23,208
Open a jar and a Then and now card writes itself out, with
its sources.

7
00:00:23,208 --> 00:00:25,004
Willow bark became aspirin.

8
00:00:25,004 --> 00:00:28,596
Every card says: history, not medical advice.

9
00:00:28,596 --> 00:00:31,483
The dangerous remedies carry a wax seal and a skull.

10
00:00:31,483 --> 00:00:36,580
Hover one, and the ghost turns sickly green while the
nearest candle gutters out.

11
00:00:36,580 --> 00:00:41,434
The poison cabinet keeps foxglove, laudanum, mercury and
arsenic behind glass,

12
00:00:41,434 --> 00:00:44,773
with a plain warning: never try any of them.

13
00:00:44,773 --> 00:00:48,209
The Ofrenda honours ten real people from pharmacy history.

14
00:00:48,209 --> 00:00:51,705
Light a candle for each, and a marigold blooms beside them.

15
00:00:51,705 --> 00:00:54,556
Light all ten, and Ambrose thanks you.

16
00:00:54,556 --> 00:00:58,061
A quiz called Remedy or Poison asks what each remedy became,

17
00:00:58,061 --> 00:01:00,648
using only the checked fact sheet.

18
00:01:00,648 --> 00:01:05,387
The ghost chat uses Gemma, an open-weight model, hosted
through the Gemini API,

19
00:01:05,387 --> 00:01:08,086
so nothing heavy runs on my laptop.

20
00:01:08,086 --> 00:01:11,359
Behind the scenes, the server gives Gemma the fact sheet,

21
00:01:11,359 --> 00:01:16,209
checks every question and every answer, and keeps my API key
off the page.

22
00:01:16,209 --> 00:01:20,015
Ask who Edward Stone was, and he answers in a few short
sentences,

23
00:01:20,015 --> 00:01:22,057
only from the fact sheet.

24
00:01:22,057 --> 00:01:24,875
Ask what to take for a headache, and he refuses,

25
00:01:24,875 --> 00:01:27,341
and sends you to a doctor or a pharmacist.

26
00:01:27,341 --> 00:01:30,935
He never gives doses and never recommends a remedy.

27
00:01:30,935 --> 00:01:32,859
Open every jar and finish the quiz,

28
00:01:32,859 --> 00:01:37,202
and the ghost writes you an Apprentice Apothecary
certificate, with a wax seal,

29
00:01:37,202 --> 00:01:38,791
ready to download.

30
00:01:38,791 --> 00:01:41,838
It works on a phone too, it respects reduced motion,

31
00:01:41,838 --> 00:01:45,719
and everything you light or write stays in your browser.

32
00:01:45,719 --> 00:01:48,549
The code is open source under the MIT license.

33
00:01:48,549 --> 00:01:53,655
Gemma's open weights made this possible, and the ghost never
leaves the fact sheet.

34
00:01:53,655 --> 00:01:55,978
History, not medical advice.

